One — phase 11, and it’s optional.

Release 1 is done. Phases 1–10 are built, committed and pushed. The definition of done you wrote is met.

Phase 11 was never a phase in the same sense — it’s the “later features, one at a time” list, meant to be picked from after release:

	Later feature
1	Topic threads — group mail, Slack and meetings about one customer or deal
2	People cards — last interactions, open items, what you owe them
3	Smart snooze — “after my 2pm”, “when they reply”
4	Reply templates with variables and rules
5	Calendar protection — back-to-back warnings, one-click focus blocks

Plus batched digests, quick-capture hotkey, and meeting lifecycle (prep before, follow-up draft after).

My recommendation: don’t start phase 11 yet. Run --live for a week first. Three things in the current build are guesses that real use will correct, and building on top of them now means building on sand:

Search ranking is untuned bm25 — demo data is too small to tell whether the ordering feels right on a real mailbox.
Commitment extraction is deterministic string matching. The shortcut: comment in summaries.py names what it misses; a week of your real sent mail tells you whether that list needs the model.
The privacy app list came from documentation, not observation. One Teams call confirms or corrects it.

Next: run it live for a few days, then tell me which of the five you want.

